            <div class="who-text">
              <p>I'm Said Mohaddes Sadeqi. I lost sight in one eye during the war in
              Afghanistan.</p>
              <p>At seventeen, in Herat, I built a wearable to help blind people move
              around a city that was not built for them. It cost about $112. We tested
              it with blind users at a support centre in Herat, and took it to
              TEKNOFEST in Turkey, where it won Best Presentation.</p>
              <p>I've been building for the same people ever since. I'm a developer at
              PIIIX, and I founded Third Eye Worldwide.</p>
              <p>Most sites treat access as something you add at the end. I treat it
              as the thing being designed. This one is the argument: everything here
              works without sight, and if that is true then the rest of what I say
              about my work is worth reading.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
